---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service" description="Terms of service for StudentKit.">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mb-8">Terms of Service</h1>
    
    <div class="prose prose-emerald text-gray-600">
      <p>Last updated: {new Date().toLocaleDateString()}</p>
      
      <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p>By accessing and using StudentKit, you accept and agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree with any part of these terms, you must not use our website.</p>
      
      <h2>2. Use of Tools</h2>
      <p>StudentKit provides free, browser-based calculators and tools for students. These tools are provided "as is" for informational and personal use only. While we strive for accuracy, you should not rely solely on these tools for critical academic decisions.</p>
      
      <h2>3. Disclaimer of Accuracy</h2>
      <p>Educational institutions have varying policies regarding grading, attendance, and GPA calculations. The formulas used on this website (such as CGPA to Percentage multipliers) are generalized. <strong>Always consult your university's official handbook or administration for official calculations.</strong> We are not responsible for any academic misunderstandings or issues arising from the use of our tools.</p>
      
      <h2>4. No Warranties</h2>
      <p>StudentKit makes no warranties, expressed or implied, regarding the website's availability, accuracy, or suitability for any particular purpose. We do not warrant that the tools will be error-free or uninterrupted.</p>
      
      <h2>5. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>In no event shall StudentKit or its creators be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, consequential, or special damages arising out of or in any way connected with the use of our website or tools.</p>
      
      <h2>6. Modifications</h2>
      <p>We reserve the right to modify or discontinue any tool or feature on StudentKit at any time without prior notice.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
